  "caption": "Quinn became a parent. By week eight the joey was heavier every day, and the thumb side of Quinn's wrist started saying nope, even to opening a bottle.\n\nScooping a baby under the arms bends the wrist with the thumb stuck out, and new parents do it many times a day with little rest and less sleep. Partners can get it too.\n\nWhat often helps: lifting with straight wrists and both hands, bringing bub close and swapping sides, easing thumb-heavy tasks like long scrolling, a thumb splint for tricky tasks, and grip and forearm strength once it settles.\n\nNumbness, tingling, weakness, severe pain, or pain that isn't easing with changes is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
